WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.315 --> 00:00:03.148
- [Mark] So, what are your names?

00:00:03.148 --> 00:00:03.981
- Ozzy.

00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:05.440
- [Kaitlin] And Kaitlin.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.273
- [Mark] Kaitlin.

00:00:06.273 --> 00:00:07.390
And where are you guys from?

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.249
- [Kaitlin] Chicago, Illinois.

00:00:08.249 --> 00:00:09.513
- [Mark] Chicago, I see.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.211
How long you guys been out here?

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.129
- [Ozzy] Maybe two and a half years.

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:15.980
- [Mark] Two and a half years in LA,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.260
and then how long on Skid Row?

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.480
Or close to here.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.749
- No in LA for two and a half years,

00:00:20.749 --> 00:00:25.011
in Skid Row we've probably been
a good seven months, right?

00:00:25.011 --> 00:00:27.942
- [Kaitlin] Yeah, sixish months probably.

00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:28.800
- Yeah, pardon my-

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.940
- Not too long,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.999
we used to stay in MacArthur Park,

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:33.790
not much better.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.926
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:36.310
Kind of the same scene.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.550
- Not much worse. (laughs)

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:38.383
- Yeah (laughs)

00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.216
- [Mark] Is it worse?

00:00:39.216 --> 00:00:40.210
- I said not much worse.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.300
- [Mark] Not much worse, right.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.133
- It's like the same,

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:45.511
not...there's more gang
activity over there

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:46.570
- [Mark] Yeah

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.210
- Yeah, here's less incorporated

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.236
- [Mark] And you guys are on the street?

00:00:53.236 --> 00:00:54.069
- Yes.

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:56.620
- [Mark] How long you been
in the cold on the street?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.323
- Me personally, just this whole time,

00:01:02.898 --> 00:01:05.136
him, like forever.

00:01:05.136 --> 00:01:06.906
- A good decade on and off

00:01:06.906 --> 00:01:08.030
- [Mark] Oh really?

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.318
- Yeah, I've gotten bunch of apartments,

00:01:09.318 --> 00:01:13.817
and you know I really
taken my time to enjoy

00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.593
and suck the juice out of like, you know,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.920
conditioned living,

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:19.753
you know what I mean,

00:01:19.753 --> 00:01:21.830
in a box with an air conditioner and stuff

00:01:23.735 --> 00:01:25.840
and then I get hungry
for the road ya know,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.447
I'm before all other things a traveler,

00:01:28.447 --> 00:01:29.860
I'm not really a...

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.420
I don't feel like sticking to
one spot is really my style,

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.010
we've just kinda got shackled
by a few things kinda here

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.000
and also

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.390
it's kind of comfortable in a way.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.680
- LA got us a little bit stuck.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:47.543
- Yeah.

00:01:49.121 --> 00:01:50.920
- We were supposed to ride freight trains

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.200
and be on this romantic
adventure and uh...

00:01:55.522 --> 00:01:58.853
- The qualms of like addiction
and what not, you know.

00:01:58.853 --> 00:02:00.261
- [Mark] What's your drug of choice?

00:02:00.261 --> 00:02:02.377
- [Ozzy And Katilin] Heroin

00:02:02.377 --> 00:02:03.540
- [Mark] Heroin? Both you guys?

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.471
- [Ozzy And Katilin] Yeah

00:02:04.471 --> 00:02:06.139
- [Mark] Yeah, heroin's a bad one.

00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:06.972
- [Ozzy] Yeah

00:02:06.972 --> 00:02:08.881
- [Kaitlin] Yeah, now its
a just straight fentanyl.

00:02:08.881 --> 00:02:13.024
We don't even bother with
the heroin part anymore.

00:02:13.024 --> 00:02:15.081
We just smoke fentanyl.

00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:15.914
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:17.339
- [Kaitlin] Yeah.

00:02:17.339 --> 00:02:19.032
- [Ozzy] It's crazy-
[Kaitlin] -it's horrible.

00:02:19.032 --> 00:02:20.812
- [Ozzy] It's crazy cuz
it's more involving,

00:02:20.812 --> 00:02:23.752
and sucks more out of you
than even intravenous use.

00:02:23.752 --> 00:02:25.604
You just smoke it and...

00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:26.747
- [Kaitlin] It's like, you know,

00:02:26.747 --> 00:02:28.171
you see crack heads on the street

00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:31.473
and you think oh crack's like probably,

00:02:31.473 --> 00:02:34.291
oh those people are the worst people.

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:38.360
Fentanyl makes you a worse crack head

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.193
than crack does I think.

00:02:39.193 --> 00:02:41.750
(Mark murmurs)

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.307
If that makes sense.

00:02:43.307 --> 00:02:45.250
- [Ozzy] I can't say it's not without

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.150
its beautiful parts though,
you know what I mean.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.300
- [Mark] What are the upsides of-

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.670
- [Ozzy] I mean, just the
time that I spend with her,

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.966
and little magic moments
you have you know,

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:58.966
that kinda completely transport
us out of this you know.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:00.930
It's still like

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.310
kind of like

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:06.302
an intoxicating little fairy
tale of it's own, you know.

00:03:06.302 --> 00:03:09.332
And just like exploring her...

00:03:09.332 --> 00:03:10.842
- [Mark] How old are you guys?

00:03:10.842 --> 00:03:12.661
- [Ozzy] I'm 28, 29. 30!

00:03:12.661 --> 00:03:13.740
- [Mark] You're 30?

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.573
- [Ozzy] Yeah.

00:03:14.573 --> 00:03:16.190
- [Kaitlin] I just turned 24.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.590
- [Mark] 24?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.993
Where would you guys like to
see yourselves in five years?

00:03:19.993 --> 00:03:24.993
- [Ozzy] Almost exactly where
I was like three years ago,

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.260
four years ago.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.360
I had a really cool apartment
with really good people,

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.497
and stuff like that.

00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:34.497
And I kinda just, I got a
tiny smudge of legal trouble,

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.168
like a smudge seriously, and...

00:03:36.168 --> 00:03:37.660
- [Mark] What kind of trouble?

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.710
- Just, I just had um...

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.550
- We sold LSD in Chicago,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.740
which holds an eight year sentence.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.460
- Yeah, but I could have beat all that,

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:49.250
I really just had a little
drug charge that snowballed,

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.097
and I just had to do drug classes for it,

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:53.590
I could never complete them,

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:54.423
so I kept getting locked up for it,

00:03:54.423 --> 00:03:56.217
it was like a yo-yo process.

00:03:56.217 --> 00:03:57.697
Knowing now what I,

00:03:57.697 --> 00:04:00.048
if I knew then what I know now,

00:04:00.048 --> 00:04:02.857
I probably would just face the music

00:04:02.857 --> 00:04:04.239
- Yeah, like go to jail

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:05.072
- It seems like...

00:04:05.072 --> 00:04:06.939
- or take prison time or whatever

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:08.169
(sirens in the background)

00:04:08.169 --> 00:04:09.520
but he kept choosing probation, and...

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.257
- It'd be like 60 days
as opposed to you know...

00:04:12.257 --> 00:04:14.009
- That's like hard to complete

00:04:14.009 --> 00:04:18.430
all of their hoops they want
you to jump through, you know.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.263
- Yeah.

00:04:19.263 --> 00:04:21.858
I thought, oh, I can't
leave her alone for 60 days,

00:04:21.858 --> 00:04:25.275
and now its kinda like it's own...

00:04:25.275 --> 00:04:28.700
- I have literally been
left alone for 60 days.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.533
- [Mark] What age were you

00:04:29.533 --> 00:04:31.860
when you guys did drugs
for the first time?

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.060
- Like, officially I'd say 16.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.299
- [Mark] And what drug was that?

00:04:37.299 --> 00:04:39.450
- LSD, yeah LSD.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.300
And then I also did,

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.339
I mean I tried heroin
when I was 16 as well.

00:04:42.339 --> 00:04:44.604
- [Mark] Oh, you did?

00:04:44.604 --> 00:04:47.343
- Yeah, kinda weird I don't know.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.000
- I, I started with the
gateway drug, weed. (laughs)

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.923
- Yeah I didn't try weed
until I was way older

00:04:55.923 --> 00:04:59.980
- Weed and alcohol, but
like that was when I was 15,

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:03.420
and I didn't do any hardcore drugs until

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.387
I basically met you, probably.

00:05:09.397 --> 00:05:10.728
- Makes sense.

00:05:10.728 --> 00:05:11.561
- It's not your fault,

00:05:11.561 --> 00:05:13.848
its just the crew we
were hanging out with was

00:05:13.848 --> 00:05:17.381
- Yeah that didn't stop-
- already addicts

00:05:17.381 --> 00:05:19.040
- I cried for three months,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.720
I was like can we please
just smoke weed today guys?

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.010
And they were already completely in the

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.430
what's it called?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.263
- Throes?

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.143
- Yeah.

00:05:31.143 --> 00:05:31.976
- Throes of like,

00:05:31.976 --> 00:05:32.809
- Addiction?

00:05:32.809 --> 00:05:33.675
- Habitual use, yeah.

00:05:33.675 --> 00:05:35.800
- I didn't start daily use
either until we started dating.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.083
But yeah, it just snowballs
so quickly, like I said.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.340
- [Mark] Tell me about your
childhood, your family.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:48.713
- Um, I came into the country at age 3,

00:05:49.593 --> 00:05:50.670
my father

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.737
was a reporter in

00:05:53.737 --> 00:05:56.810
El Salvador. Correspondence work

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:00.132
for Time Magazine and stuff,
covering the war out there.

00:06:00.132 --> 00:06:03.930
He's named after Oscar Romero,
the archbishop of El Salvador

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.800
at the time, he was assassinated,
he was like a close friend

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.800
of my family's and stuff. And
yeah I don't know, and then

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:15.850
my mom, like, all of our
assets were seized by the

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.493
Salvadorian government,
we fled to Mexico, fled

00:06:18.493 --> 00:06:21.291
to this country, my mom
worked to build a life for us

00:06:21.291 --> 00:06:24.943
and when I was like, eleven,
she kind of, you know,

00:06:24.943 --> 00:06:29.943
had everything put together,
and we just continued life,

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.053
me and my brother, her, my brother, and I,

00:06:35.646 --> 00:06:37.150
and, it was pretty
perfect, I'm not gonna lie.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:41.327
It worked, it was good, a
really loving mother, and yeah.

00:06:42.558 --> 00:06:43.773
How about you?

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:51.439
- Well, my mom had me out of
wedlock, and when I was three,

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.470
three or four, she married my step-dad,

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.883
and when I was like, ten-ish,

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:06.210
my mom moved to Chicago, she got pregnant

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:10.250
with twins, my little brother
and sister. They're like,

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.886
my step-siblings, but really
they're just my siblings.

00:07:12.886 --> 00:07:15.463
And my step-dad's really just my dad.

00:07:17.579 --> 00:07:19.050
My step-dad's kind of

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.660
an asshole, he never drank or anything,

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:26.660
he just had like, habitual
verbal abuse problems, mostly.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.890
It became physical when
I was like, eleven.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:31.723
- [Mark] With you?

00:07:31.723 --> 00:07:36.291
- Yeah, uh, and that, you know,
like I grew up in a really,

00:07:36.291 --> 00:07:39.313
really nice community on
the North Shore of Chicago,

00:07:40.604 --> 00:07:43.404
and that just sort of threw
me into a sort of rebellious

00:07:45.344 --> 00:07:47.243
phase I guess?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.570
And so I started hanging out with

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:55.570
the wrong crowd, so to speak,
the Kids Without Dads club.

00:07:56.368 --> 00:07:58.384
(laughing)

00:07:58.384 --> 00:07:59.217
- The Lost Boys.

00:07:59.217 --> 00:08:00.683
- Yeah, stuff like that.

00:08:02.668 --> 00:08:05.010
I don't know. I had a
really good family too.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:10.010
I didn't come from anything
dirt poor, or anything like

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:13.663
super bad.

00:08:13.663 --> 00:08:15.320
- [Mark] No like, sexual
abuse or anything like that?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:16.153
- No.

00:08:22.187 --> 00:08:24.337
I think, I don't know,
I'm not really sure.

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.637
- [Mark] You guys are happy
with your situation right now?

00:08:30.637 --> 00:08:33.412
- Not at all, not at all.
We want to quit every day,

00:08:33.412 --> 00:08:35.651
we get into fights over it all the time.

00:08:35.651 --> 00:08:40.651
He just found a rehab that,
Medicali doesn't pay for

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.970
medical, like, withdrawal.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:46.803
- Medical detoxing.

00:08:46.803 --> 00:08:50.245
- Yeah, we need a medical
detox. That's just a fact.

00:08:50.245 --> 00:08:53.265
- We've been going through
detoxes and rehabs,

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.850
not going through them
physically but just like,

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.066
calling, on the internet.

00:08:57.066 --> 00:08:59.504
- I've physically, I've
physically gone through

00:08:59.504 --> 00:09:01.135
like, one and a half.

00:09:01.135 --> 00:09:02.370
- No, no, but did you-

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.203
- No, but in Chicago-

00:09:03.203 --> 00:09:05.620
- But in Chicago I had
gone into a couple rehabs.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.627
But that was when I was
17 man, super indifferent

00:09:08.627 --> 00:09:10.857
about the results, you know.

00:09:10.857 --> 00:09:12.325
- [Mark] You see what the
future is down the road

00:09:12.325 --> 00:09:13.187
for this, right?

00:09:13.187 --> 00:09:14.020
- Yeah.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.236
- Uh, it's right outside.

00:09:15.236 --> 00:09:20.145
- [Mark] Look around,
it's not a pretty picture.

00:09:20.145 --> 00:09:23.456
- Well I mean I knew when I
watched Requiem for a Dream,

00:09:23.456 --> 00:09:24.810
what I was kind of, in
a sense, signing up for,

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:29.810
but now there's a big part
of me that, ah, is growing

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:34.873
and growing and kind
of trying to take back

00:09:34.873 --> 00:09:38.860
the steering wheel of my
life, build something,

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.510
build a nest for us and whatnot.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.343
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:09:41.343 --> 00:09:42.265
- Yeah.

00:09:42.265 --> 00:09:43.223
- [Mark] Well, good luck with that.

00:09:43.223 --> 00:09:44.056
- Appreciate it.

00:09:44.056 --> 00:09:44.889
- [Mark] Thank you so
much for talking with me.

00:09:44.889 --> 00:09:45.722
- Absolutely.

00:09:45.722 --> 00:09:46.912
You're easy to talk to.

00:09:46.912 --> 00:09:48.509
- [Mark] I'll give you a
ride back to your place.

00:09:48.509 --> 00:09:49.342
- All right

00:09:49.342 --> 00:09:50.259
- Thank you

